{"ocrText": "many repercussions from the plan Nicole and\nI had to solve my\nproblems with my lady friend,\nI would have saved myself, as well\nas others, the misery we have all had to endure because of the pic-\nture-taking incident. Now that\nit\nis clear beyond any doubt that\nnothing was amiss between Nicole and me,\nI hope that your feel-\nings toward me will once again be kind. As you know,\nI\nleft my\neasel and sketch pad\nat your house. Of course shipping the easel\nwould be too much trouble, but\nI would appreciate\nit very much if\nmy sketchbook could be sent to me. The sketches of Nicole are\nimportant, and the project must go on quite apart from our per-\nsonal problems.\nIf you would send the sketchbook to me,\nI\nwill\nsend you a check by return mail to reimburse you for your trouble.\nI hope that you are having a pleasant summer.\nBest wishes,\nEdward\nDear Lucy,\nI've been trying all summer to get up the nerve to ask you out,\nbut I've never been able to do it.\nI thought that maybe you thought\nI wasn't your type, because\nI work at the nursery.\nI do know that\nyou were flirting with me the day you and your friend were there,\nthough.\nI hope\nI don't insult you by saying this. What's wrong\nwith flirting, after all.\nI was very interested and\nI guess it's a sign of\nhow much ego\nI have that\nI thought you'd come by\nagain, or\nmaybe even call.\nI did meet your friend who wanted to buy trees\nfor his front lawn because he wanted to make his house, which was\nup for sale, look nice.\nI told him to say hello. Maybe he did.\nI suppose\nI should write Cindi Coeur instead of Lucy Spenser,\nbut that might be a little too cute.\nI thought you could answer my\nquestion just as well.\nI guess I'm writing you because\nI think you'll give me an honest\nanswer. Did you also feel good energy between us, and if so, is the\nreason you stayed away because you're involved with someone\nelse or because\nI was an employee at a nursery? I'm going to con-\nfide in you:\nI need to know, because my luck has been lousy lately.\nMy father is quite rich, and\nI always felt that\nif\nI didn't do some-\nthing real with my summers\n(I realize that working in a nursery\nisn't meaningful, but other summers I've done things like work at a\ncamp for handicapped kids), I'd become just another one of those\nkids who lounge around their parents' summer house, doing some\nperfunctory\nlittle things the gardener or whoever doesn't do, and\nsipping gin and tonics with the folks at night.\nI don't mean to pre-\nsent myself as some prince in frog's clothing, but\nit would help me\n203", "textLayer": [{"text": "many", "x": 9.72, "y": 5.33, "w": 5.97, "h": 1.89, "fontSize": 9.4}, {"text": "repercussions", "x": 17.11, "y": 5.62, "w": 15.02, "h": 1.46, "fontSize": 7.3}, {"text": "from", "x": 33.41, "y": 5.48, "w": 5.21, "h": 1.65, "fontSize": 8.2}, {"text": "the", "x": 39.86, "y": 5.63, "w": 3.32, "h": 1.4, "fontSize": 7.0}, {"text": "plan", "x": 44.41, "y": 5.59, "w": 4.6, "h": 1.45, "fontSize": 7.3}, {"text": "Nicole", "x": 50.33, "y": 5.52, "w": 7.35, "h": 1.55, "fontSize": 7.7}, {"text": "and", "x": 58.86, "y": 5.46, "w": 3.89, "h": 1.64, "fontSize": 8.2}, {"text": "I", "x": 64.08, "y": 6.1, "w": 0.62, "h": 0.78, "fontSize": 3.9}, {"text": "had", "x": 66.02, "y": 5.48, "w": 3.89, "h": 1.64, "fontSize": 8.2}, {"text": "to", "x": 71.14, "y": 5.75, "w": 2.04, "h": 1.29, "fontSize": 6.4}, {"text": "solve", "x": 74.41, "y": 5.65, "w": 5.45, "h": 1.38, "fontSize": 6.9}, {"text": "my", "x": 81.09, "y": 5.14, "w": 3.32, "h": 2.1, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "problems", "x": 9.67, "y": 7.37, "w": 10.28, "h": 1.63, "fontSize": 8.1}, {"text": "with", "x": 21.0, "y": 7.42, "w": 4.93, "h": 1.56, "fontSize": 7.8}, {"text": "my", "x": 26.97, "y": 6.99, "w": 3.37, "h": 2.13, "fontSize": 10.6}, {"text": "lady", "x": 31.42, "y": 7.52, "w": 4.5, "h": 1.42, "fontSize": 7.1}, {"text": "friend,", "x": 37.11, "y": 7.61, "w": 7.2, "h": 1.3, "fontSize": 6.5}, {"text": "I